Interesting comments and a lot of good points. I agree that the ultimate 
purpose of a game be that the person playing is being entertained rather 
than frustrated. Things like permadeath can be newbie unfriendly. It would 
be really nice to take the route that Diablo II does here and allow a 
"hardcore" and "normal" setting to be toggled - permadeath only being 
enabled in the "hardcore" setting. It's a hard line to tred, though, between 
entertaining the player, and boring the player because the game is too easy. 
I mean, ideally you would be constantly challenged and engaged throughout 
the game. Eventually you would want the game to get more difficult, right? 
Then getting to a lower level than you ever have before becomes an 
accomplishment rather than something that occurs by fait. I'd be interested 
in hearing your thoughts on this as I am in the midst of starting my own 
roguelike with an emphasis on user-friendliness (mainly GUI-wise, though I'm 
against instadeath effects as I believe they lead to a poor gameplay 
experience).

